Implement Upgrade-35 as a bounded observability and scheduler-contract slice for cvsz/zcoder.

Objective: make Upgrade-34 one-shot maintenance campaigns observable and directly consumable by workers/schedulers without adding a recurring loop or a second telemetry stack.

Requirements:
- define a typed, finite, secret-free maintenance campaign event contract;
- emit started, recommendations-discovered, and exactly one completed-or-halted event per campaign;
- add a scheduler-friendly run_maintenance_campaign_once() contract returning structured report plus deterministic exit code;
- keep recurrence external to the campaign service;
- make event delivery best-effort so telemetry failures cannot change engineering state;
- count observer failures in the report while logging only exception type, not potentially sensitive exception messages;
- reuse existing ZCoderMetrics/OpenTelemetry infrastructure;
- add bounded-cardinality metrics for campaigns, recommendations, work seeded, completed/blocked/pending items, observer errors, and duration;
- never use campaign IDs as Prometheus labels; correlation IDs may exist in trace attributes only;
- include maintenance metrics in the existing Prometheus exposition;
- keep existing JSON/SQLite/PostgreSQL campaign backend behavior and DATABASE_URL handling unchanged;
- add focused unit tests for event ordering, scheduler exit codes, observer failure semantics, secret-free events, metrics, and Prometheus exposition;
- preserve Upgrade-20 execution authority, Upgrade-24 safety budgets, Upgrade-33 PostgreSQL fencing/exclusivity, local-only push default, and every existing CI/security gate.
